& [SemanticContract] is role qualified
  + supplied means caller-provided at an earlier pure boundary and never physical origin
  + inventory means the complete member sequence of the supplied assembly and never complete physical enumeration
  + ordered means the assembly's existing root-first structural sequence and never Windows, Git, traversal, or temporal order
  + canonical means unique bytes only under the exact encoding profile and never canonical filesystem path or Unicode equivalence
  + digest means aggregate SHA-256 and never signature, MAC, Merkle root, receipt, proof of possession, or authorization token
  + commitment means deterministic collision-resistant reference to the encoded subject and never witness or trust authority
  + complete is always qualified as observation fields, retained assembly, or supplied sequence
  + same encoded subject requires the same exact encoding profile and ordinary SHA-256 collision assumptions

& [PlanContract] is strict and bounded
  + [type] is WindowsSuppliedOrderedTopologyInventoryDigestPlan
  + exact result profile, exact encoding profile, and nonzero u64 commitment_identity
  + encoded plan maximum is 4096 bytes before strict JSON decoding
  + serde denies unknown, missing, malformed, overlong, wrong-profile, wrong-encoding-profile, and zero-identity input
  + immutable getters expose profile, encoding_profile, and commitment_identity
  - never: include supplied digest, observations, assembly members, limits, deadline, physical claim, receipt, or admission decision

& [InputContract] accepts one complete capability only
  + public transform accepts plan bytes and WindowsSuppliedTopologyInventoryAssembly by value
  + assembly is consumed into success only after every pure validation and encoding gate passes
  + immutable member and observation getters provide the exact subject order
  - never: accept raw observations, member vectors, individual carriers, carrier fragments, caller-declared digest, or deserialized success output

& [EvaluationContract] is fail closed and ordered
  + reject oversized or malformed plan before decoding success
  + require exact plan profiles and nonzero commitment identity
  + require exact assembly profile
  + convert ordered member length exactly to u64 and require assembly entry_count equality
  + rerun current ValidateTopologyForm for every member observation
  + require first observation RootDirectory with None relative_path
  + require every later observation not RootDirectory and with Some relative_path
  + require every observation_ordinal equal its checked one-based sequence position
  + recompute regular-file length sum with checked arithmetic and require exact total_file_bytes equality
  + stream exact canonical records into one new SHA-256 accumulator
  + finalize exactly one lowercase 64-hex digest
  + return one output retaining exact plan and complete assembly
  + first failure returns no digest result or partial canonical bytes

& [CanonicalPrimitiveEncoding] is architecture independent
  + u32 is exactly four big-endian bytes
  + u64 is exactly eight big-endian bytes
  + enum is exactly one declared nonzero byte and never a language discriminant or serializer label
  + option is exactly 0x00 for absent or 0x01 followed by the value for present
  + text is u64 big-endian UTF-8 byte count followed by exact UTF-8 bytes
  + sequence is u64 big-endian element count followed by each element
  + file identity is validated lowercase 32-hex decoded to exactly 16 bytes
  + content digest is validated lowercase 64-hex decoded to exactly 32 bytes
  + every field begins with one declared nonzero field tag
  + every observation begins with one declared entry-start tag
  - never: use native integer layout, usize, JSON, CBOR, Debug, serde field order, locale, normalization, padding, or implicit delimiter

& [CanonicalTagTable] is closed
  + [entry_start] is 0x01
  + [relative_path] is 0x10
  + [kind] is 0x11
  + [mode_class] is 0x12
  + [attributes] is 0x13
  + [volume_serial] is 0x14
  + [file_id] is 0x15
  + [number_of_links] is 0x16
  + [streams] is 0x17
  + [length] is 0x18
  + [content_sha256] is 0x19
  + [observation_ordinal] is 0x1A
  + [root_directory_kind] is 0x01
  + [directory_kind] is 0x02
  + [regular_file_kind] is 0x03
  + [directory_mode] is 0x01
  + [regular_non_executable_mode] is 0x02
  + [regular_executable_mode] is 0x03
  + [stream_start] is 0x20
  + [stream_name] is 0x21
  + [stream_size] is 0x22
  + [stream_kind] is 0x23
  + [unnamed_default_stream_kind] is 0x01
  + [named_data_stream_kind] is 0x02
  + all unlisted and alternate tags reject at any future separately governed decoder boundary

& [CanonicalSequenceContract] is exact
  + exact ASCII encoding profile followed by one zero byte
  + one u64 big-endian assembly entry count
  + each observation in the assembly's existing order
  + entry-start
  + relative_path tag and option-encoded text
  + kind tag and explicit kind byte
  + mode_class tag and explicit mode byte
  + attributes tag and u32
  + volume_serial tag and u64
  + file_id tag and decoded 16 bytes
  + number_of_links tag and u32
  + streams tag, u64 count, and each stream record in existing validated order
  + each stream is stream-start, name tag and text, size tag and u64, kind tag and explicit stream-kind byte
  + length tag and option-encoded u64
  + content_sha256 tag and option-encoded decoded 32 bytes
  + observation_ordinal tag and u64
  + each semantic field and optional presence occurs exactly once

& [DigestSubjectContract] separates record content from retained derivation
  + included are encoding domain, entry count, member order, and every TopologyEntryObservation and TopologyStreamFact semantic field
  + excluded are all plans, limits, deadlines, correlation identities, projection identities, entry references, carrier profiles, preflight, stability, content-read process records, and proof lineage
  + excluded lineage remains fully owned inside the retained assembly
  + plan or carrier-only lineage changes may change result serialization while leaving ordered_inventory_sha256 unchanged
  - never: return a digest detached from the complete assembly that formed its supplied subject

& [StreamingContract] is bounded by subject structure
  + one private subject-local writer owns Sha256
  + fixed-width values use stack arrays
  + text writes length and existing UTF-8 slices without copying the complete inventory
  + validated file identities and content digests decode through fixed 16-byte and 32-byte arrays
  + no complete canonical byte vector, duplicate observation collection, public encoder, decoder, or migration surface exists
  + sha2 is the existing workspace dependency and Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock remain unchanged

& [OutputContract] is nonforgeable and lineage preserving
  + [type] is WindowsSuppliedOrderedTopologyInventoryDigest
  + private fields are profile, encoding_profile, plan, assembly, and ordered_inventory_sha256
  + derives Serialize but not Deserialize or Default
  + immutable getters expose the exact fields
  + no public field, mutable getter, public success constructor, From, Into, alternate decoder, or raw success path exists

& [FaultContract] is closed, bounded, nested, and atomic
  + [type] is WindowsSuppliedOrderedTopologyInventoryDigestFault
  + [codes] are json, profile, commitment_identity, encoding_profile, topology_form, assembly, count, ordinal, accounting, hex, arithmetic, resource, and internal
  + field is at most 64 Unicode scalars and message at most 256 Unicode scalars
  + exact TopologyFormFault is present only when code is topology_form
  + no fault contains partial digest, canonical bytes, full observation, carrier, assembly, or lower success record
  + no failure returns a digest result

& [EvidenceContract] is honest
  + supplied retains lower epistemic origin
  + carrier_projected retains completed output-only carrier grade
  + structurally_assembled retains bounded ordered supplied-set grade
  + current_revalidated records current observation and assembly-correlation checks at this boundary
  + canonically_committed records exact supplied ordered observation bytes under the exact encoding profile
  + physically_observed, enumerated_complete, temporally_repeated, quiescent_double_inventory, receipted, and admitted are absent

& [EffectContract] is zero
  + deterministic in-memory validation, canonical updates, hashing, and result construction only
  + no unsafe, Windows API, filesystem, path resolution, process, environment, clock, randomness, network, persistence, database, model, Git, tool, fixture, traversal, mutation, seal, test-execution effect, cleanup, or promotion
  + physical and effect-bearing builders and tests remain uninvoked

& [RequirementSet] is atomic
  + [M2B-SOTID-001] strict bounded plan with exact commitment and encoding profiles
  + [M2B-SOTID-002] complete output-only assembly input only
  + [M2B-SOTID-003] current M2A revalidation for every ordered observation
  + [M2B-SOTID-004] exact assembly count, root-first, kind, path, and ordinal correlations
  + [M2B-SOTID-005] checked total regular-file byte accounting correlation
  + [M2B-SOTID-006] exact domain separator and entry-count commitment
  + [M2B-SOTID-007] fixed big-endian integer and explicit enum-tag encoding
  + [M2B-SOTID-008] explicit option, text, digest, identity, sequence, field, entry, and stream framing
  + [M2B-SOTID-009] every observation and stream semantic field committed
  + [M2B-SOTID-010] policy, correlation, carrier-profile, and proof-lineage exclusion from digest subject
  + [M2B-SOTID-011] bounded streaming SHA-256 without whole-inventory encoding allocation
  + [M2B-SOTID-012] private Serialize-only output retaining complete assembly and digest
  + [M2B-SOTID-013] closed bounded fault vocabulary and atomic failure
  + [M2B-SOTID-014] zero effects, unsafe, platform calls, dependencies, and lockfile delta
  + [M2B-SOTID-015] focused vectors, static boundary, global regression, evidence, audit, rollback, and provenance proof

& [VerificationContract] is independent and proportional
  + root-only and mixed nested inventories have exact known reference digests
  + at least one expected digest is reproduced from test-only manually assembled canonical bytes independent from production writer helpers
  + every fixed-width, enum, optional, text, identity, digest, sequence, stream, count, and member-order class has a sensitivity proof
  + plan correlation and carrier-only lineage have intentional-exclusion proofs while retained results differ
  + every plan, form, assembly, count, ordinal, accounting, hex, arithmetic, resource, and bounded diagnostic gate has denial proof
  + static tests reject Deserialize, Default, public fields, public success construction, From, Into, raw input, public canonical bytes, JSON hashing, alternate hash dependency, unsafe, platform, filesystem, and effect surfaces
  + focused debug and overflow-checked release, workspace debug and overflow-checked release, format, warnings-denied lint, release build, warnings-denied docs, dependency audit, recursive evidence, provenance review, rollback, and clean tree must pass
  + no physical or effect-bearing test may be invoked

& [ImplementationBoundary] is one pure subject-local slice
  + one module, one lib export, module tests, one independent static integration test, evidence manifest, solution, completion review, proof, narrative, reentry, and recursive evidence updates
  + private helpers may separate validation, fixed-width hex decode, tag writing, observation writing, and stream writing
  + public API remains one transform plus immutable data getters
  + Cargo and lockfile delta are zero

& [RollbackContract] is exact
  + remove only the new module, export, static test, evidence manifest, and derived closure records
  + retain source, SJS artifacts, faults, and proof history
  + rollback never changes an existing digest meaning or activates another profile

& [StopBoundary] is mandatory
  + stop on any source or prerequisite hash drift
  + stop on hidden default, serializer-dependent representation, native endianness, unspecified tag, omitted field, normalization, sorting, repair, whole-inventory buffer, or digest-subject ambiguity
  + stop on public success forgeability, new dependency, unsafe, platform call, filesystem call, effect, stale evidence, or failed proof
  + stop on any claim of physical origin, enumeration completeness, freshness, temporal equality, quiescence, receipt, admission, mutation, or promotion

& [SJSProcessingTrace] is complete
  + source preserved separately and byte bound
  + subject delineated and exploded into a separate artifact
  + overloaded terms semantically refined
  + C01 through C20 source checked and reapplied
  + P01 through P08 pruned and G01 through G05 dispositioned
  + seven distinct edge probes phase locked
  + data identity, relation, cardinality, transform, state, lifecycle, physical representation, and provenance checked
  + justification, plan, registry, requirement matrix, build slice, and pre-signature phase lock separately recorded and hash bound

